PTX MP+vector-release
"A vector store is a set of scalar stores in an unspecified order (6569): with .release, the element on y need not follow the element on x, so y = 1 does not imply x = 1. D43 makes a strong vector of at most 16 bytes single-copy atomic, which constrains a vector read of the elements, not two scalar reads. Expected: allowed."
{
x=0;
y=0;
P1:r0=0;
P1:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,gpu 0               | P1@cta 1,gpu 0       ;
 st.release.gpu.v2 x, y, 1, 1 | ld.acquire.gpu r0, y ;
                              | ld.relaxed.gpu r1, x ;
exists
(P1:r0 == 1 /\ P1:r1 == 0)
